  "shipped_smoke": {
    "recorded_at": "2026-09-25",
    "why": "The `models` array below is the 0.1.0 pilot proof and is kept as evidence: its TTS entry, Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-0.6B-CustomVoice-8bit, was cut from the catalog in ST-13.B, so `packaging/smoke_voice.py` planned a run around a model the packaged catalogue no longer offers and reported the TTS role as unexercised. This key names a model the catalogue still ships, with the smoke parameters that model itself publishes, and it is what the smoke now plans and verifies from.",
    "smoke_params_note": "Qwen3-TTS Base publishes no preset-speaker roster - the `qwen3_preset_speakers` roster in `generation.py` belongs to the CustomVoice family, which this catalog does not ship - so no `preset_speaker` is recorded here. The parameters are the request fields this model's own catalog row publishes: `en` is one of its ten languages, and `seed` is the worker's own sampling control (the historical pilot used 42).",
    "asr_note": "The Whisper entry is recorded here too because the historical one no longer describes what is installed: its file list carries `.gitattributes` and `README.md`, which the app's package import does not copy into the Hugging Face cache, so `--models-dir ~/StudioHubModels` failed validation before the run. This entry is the shipped `model-manifests/whisper-turbo.json` package, which is exactly what `~/StudioHubModels/whisper-turbo/<revision>/` holds.",
    "reference_note": "Qwen3-TTS Base clones: the worker refuses a request that carries neither a Voices-library id nor a private reference. The reference below is the project's tracked qual/evidence clip, the same one the stored r07 clone probes staged for this exact checkpoint (qualification/evidence/r07-2026-09-21/qwen06-base-8bit.json). `smoke()` uploads it for this repo only, through the worker's own POST /api/generate/txt2speech/reference.",
